    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is most probably a quirk of the elaboration order</p>",
        "id": 599750979,
        "sender_full_name": "Yaël Dillies",
        "timestamp": 1780481252
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, I don't have a precise understanding, but I can see looking at the errors/infotrees that we're left with mvars that disappear upon having <code>by</code>.</p>",
        "id": 599751364,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1780481362
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"387244\">Yaël Dillies</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/by.20exact.20can.27t.20be.20removed/near/599750979\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>It is most probably a quirk of the elaboration order</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I mean, sure. The question is why. </p>\n<p>Claude <span aria-label=\"robot\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f916\" role=\"img\" title=\"robot\">:robot:</span> says (summarised by me): the elaborator handles an absent autoParam by <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/02b6c1a92a7a5092e5e5a039c8961273981e03e2/src/Lean/Elab/App.lean#L846\">creating a metavariable</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/02b6c1a92a7a5092e5e5a039c8961273981e03e2/src/Lean/Elab/Term/TermElabM.lean#L1445\">marking it as synthetic opaque</a>. Because the metavariable is synthetic opaque, unification is forbidden from assigning it (<code>isDefEq</code> won't work) and it can only be solved by running the registered tactic <code>volume_tac</code>. In term mode, <code>one_mem' := MeasurePreserving.id _</code> is elaborated eagerly against the expected type, currently <code>1 ∈ {ϕ | MeasurePreserving ⇑ϕ ?a ?b}</code>, before <code>volume_tac</code> has run. The funny thing is that <code>MeasurePreserving.id</code> has type <code>MeasurePreserving id μ μ</code> i.e. the same measure in both slots, so Lean is now faced with the unification task <code>?a = ?b</code> and these are different synthetic opaque metavariables so this fails. Similarly <code>comp</code> needs to unify two of the four synthetic opaque metavariables and this also fails.</p>\n<p>The reason <code>by exact</code> fixes it is that <code>by exact _</code> is apparently a synthetic tactic mvar, so the field is postponed, and by the time it runs, <code>synthesizeSyntheticMVars</code> has already fired the <code>volume_tac</code> tactics making the problem go away.</p>\n<p>So in fact (if all that AI-generated nonsense above is to be believed, and I'm certainly not vouching for it personally), at least part of the problem is not that there is one autoparam but that there is two!</p>",
